### Observation
The `Server: Kestrel` response header discloses the underlying web server/framework on every
response (200 and 404 alike). No `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` hardening header is present
either. Neither is a functional defect, but both are avoidable stack-disclosure /
missing-hardening items per OWASP API Security passive-checklist guidance.
